# Application Form — Boilerplate Answers

These answers are reused verbatim across every Greenhouse / Ashby / Lever / Workday
form. Each role's report has a `## Section G` block with the role-specific copy
(cover letter, why-company, why-role, salary, spotlight, additional-info). Use
this file for everything else.

> **Setup**: copy this template to `section-g-boilerplate.md` (which is
> gitignored), then fill in your real values. The auto-fill engine
> (`scripts/lib/parse-boilerplate.mjs`) reads the active file at runtime.

Last updated: {{DATE}}

---

## 1. Identity

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| First name | {{FIRST_NAME_LEGAL}} |
| Preferred / common name | {{PREFERRED_NAME}} |
| Last name | {{LAST_NAME}} |
| Email | {{EMAIL}} |
| Phone | {{PHONE}} |
| Address / Location | {{CITY}}, {{STATE}}, {{COUNTRY}} |
| LinkedIn | {{LINKEDIN_URL}} |
| GitHub | {{GITHUB_URL}} |
| Portfolio / Website | {{PORTFOLIO_URL}} |
| Pronouns | {{PRONOUNS}} |

> **Naming policy** (encoded in `scripts/lib/answer-resolver.mjs` IDENTITY_PATTERNS):
> - Default `First Name` slot → **{{PREFERRED_NAME}}** (the public, daily-use name).
> - When the form **also** has a separate `Preferred / Common / Nick / Chosen / Display Name` field, the bare `First Name` slot is treated as legal → **{{FIRST_NAME_LEGAL}}**, and the preferred slot gets **{{PREFERRED_NAME}}**. Detected by `ctx.hasPreferredNameField` in `fill-form.mjs`.
> - When the form **explicitly** says "Legal first name" / "First name as on passport" / "Government-issued first name" → **{{FIRST_NAME_LEGAL}}**. Caught by `first_name_legal` regex in resolver.
> - `Last name` is always **{{LAST_NAME}}**.
> - Cover letter, "why <company>", emails, etc. always sign as **{{PREFERRED_NAME}} {{LAST_NAME}}**.

